<title>AUSTRALIA: TENNIS-AUSTRALIAN OPEN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-AUSTRALIAN OPEN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the second day of the US$7.6 million Australian Open tennis tournament on Tuesday (prefix denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Men's singles, first round:</p>
<p>16-Alberto Berasategui (Spain) beat Todd Larkham (Australia) 6-1 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>Arnaud Boetsch (France) beat David Caldwell (U.S.) 6-0 6-0 6-2</p>
<p>8-Wayne Ferreira (South Africa) beat Carlos Costa (Spain) 6-3 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Filip Dewulf (Belgium) beat Fernon Wibier (Netherlands) 6-4 6-2 7-5</p>
<p>Michael Joyce (U.S.) beat Roberto Carretero (Spain) 6-1 7-6 (7-4) 6-1</p>
<p>Sergi Bruguera (Spain) beat Lleyton Hewitt (Australia) 6-3 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Nicklas Kulti (Sweden) beat Karim Alami (Morocco) 6-4 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>Magnus Larsson (Sweden) beat Juan Albert Viloca (Spain) 6-3 6-3 7-6 (7-3)</p>
<p>MaliVai Washington (U.S.) beat Jacco Eltingh (Netherlands) 6-3 6-7 (6-8) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>9-Marcelo Rios (Chile) beat Petr Korda (Czech Republic) 7-6 (7-4) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Peter Tramacchi (Australia) beat Johan van Herck (Belgium) 6-7 (6-8) 6-3 6-4 3-2 retired</p>
<p>Jiri Novak (Czech Republic) beat Lars Jonsson (Sweden) 6-3 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Sargis Sargsian (Armenia) beat Marcos Ondruska (South Africa) 7-6 (8-6) 7-5 4-6 6-2</p>
<p>Mark Woodforde (Australia) beat Michael Tebbutt (Australia) 6-4 6-4 7-5</p>
<p>Jonas Bjorkman (Sweden) beat Bohdan Ulihrach (Czech Republic) 1-6 6-1 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Lionel Roux (France) beat Jonathan Stark (U.S.) 1-6 4-6 7-6 (7-4) 6-2 13-11</p>
<p>Scott Draper (Australia) beat Alex Radulescu (Germany) 6-2 6-4 6-7(4-7) 6-3</p>
<p>Hernan Gumy (Argentina) beat Orlin Stanoytchev (Bulgaria) 6-4 6-4 6-4</p>
<p>Marc Rosset (Switzerland) beat Javier Sanchez (Spain) 6-4 7-6 (9-7) 6-1</p>
<p>Jan Kroslak (Slovakia) beat Andrea Gaudenzi (Italy) 4-6 6-4 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>1-Pete Sampras (U.S.) beat Dinu Pescariu (Romania) 6-2 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Leander Paes (India) beat Jaymon Crabb (Australia) 6-4 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>3-Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia) beat Ben Ellwood (Australia) 6-2 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Adrian Voinea (Romania) beat Hendrik Dreekmann (Germany) 6-2 6-1 4-6 6-4</p>
<p>Women's singles, first round:</p>
<p>Flora Perfetti (Italy) beat Katarina Studenikova (Slovakia) 6-4 7-6 (7-1)</p>
<p>5-Anke Huber (Germany) beat Amy Frazier (U.S.) 0-6 6-2 7-5</p>
<p>Lisa Raymond (U.S.) beat Siobhan Drake-Brockman (Australia) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>4-Martina Hingis (Switzerland) beat Barbara Rittner (Germany) 6-1 7-5</p>
<p>Rita Grande (Italy) beat Angeles Montolio (Spain) 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>7-Lindsay Davenport (U.S.) beat Nathalie Dechy (France) 4-6 6-1 6-1</p>
<p>Meilen Tu (U.S.) beat Lenka Cenkova (Czech Republic) 3-6 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Kristie Boogert (Netherlands) beat Nicole Arendt (U.S.) 3-6 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Wang Shi-Ting (Taiwan) beat Linda Wild (U.S.) 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Jolene Watanabe (U.S.) beat Jennifer Capriati (U.S.) 6-2 3-6 6-4</p>
<p>Francesca Lubiani (Italy) beat Rachel McQuillan (Australia) 6-2 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>Silvia Farina (Italy) beat Aleksandra Olsza (Poland) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Magdalena Grzybowska (Poland) beat Sarah Pitkowski (France) 4-6 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Dominique van Roost (Belgium) beat Bettina Fulco-Villella (Argentina) 6-0 6-3  </p>
<p>Men's singles, first round</p>
<p>11-Jim Courier (U.S.) beat Sjeng Schalken (Netherlands) 6-7 (4-7) 6-3 4-6 6-1 8-6</p>
<p>Christian Ruud (Norway) beat 13-Jan Siemerink (Netherlands) 3-6 4-6 7-5 6-2 10-8</p>
<p>Slava Dosedel (Czech Republic) beat Guy Forget (France) 6-2 3-6 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>Neville Godwin (South Africa) beat Andrei Chesnokov (Russia) 6-1 6-3 3-6 6-1</p>
<p>Karol Kucera (Slovakia) beat Paul Haarhuis (Netherlands) 6-1 3-6 6-3 4-6 6-4</p>
<p>Jeff Tarango (U.S.) beat Bryan Shelton (U.S.) 2-6 7-6 (7-1) 7-6 (7-2) 6-2</p>
<p>Marc Goellner (Germany) beat Kenneth Carlsen (Denmark) 6-4 6-1 6-7 (2-7) 6-4</p>
<p>Women's singles, first round</p>
<p>Patty Schnyder (Switzerland) beat 6-Iva Majoli (Croatia) 7-5 6-1</p>
<p>8-Irina Spirlea (Romania) beat Naoko Kijimuta (Japan) 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>9-Karina Habsudova (Slovakia) beat Silvija Talaja (Croatia) 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>14-Mary Joe Fernandez (U.S.) beat Laura Golarsa (Italy) 6-2 4-6 6-2</p>
<p>15-Chanda Rubin (U.S.) beat Radka Zrubakova (Slovakia) 7-6 (9-7) 6-3</p>
<p>Yuka Yoshida (Japan) beat Katrina Adams (U.S.) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Sandrine Testud (France) beat Elena Wagner (Germany) 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Alexandra Fusai (France) beat Ginger Helgeson Nielsen (U.S.) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Yayuk Basuki (Indonesia) beat Naoko Sawamatsu (Japan) 6-3 4-1 (retired)</p>
<p>Paola Suarez (Argentina) beat Karin Kschwendt (Austria) 7-6 (9-7) 6-3</p>
